+# Reusable UI components
+
+This application uses browser-native ES modules and custom elements, with no build step.
+
+## Coffee card
+
+Import `coffee-card.js` once, then supply a product object:
+
+```js
+import './components/coffee-card.js';
+const card = document.createElement('coffee-card');
+card.product = {
+  id: 'house', name: 'House Coffee', price: 3.50,
+  description: 'Your everyday favorite.', notes: 'Smooth · Balanced',
+  badge: 'HOUSE FAVORITE', image: '/coffee.jpg', alt: 'A cup of coffee'
+};
+document.querySelector('.product-grid').append(card);
+```
+
+Listen for the bubbling `product-select` event; its `detail` contains the product. Set `card.product` again to update an existing card. Product strings must come from trusted application data.
+
+## Modal
+
+`createModal(dialogElement, contentElement)` returns `show(trustedMarkup)` and `close()`. Provide a native `<dialog>` containing a `[data-close-modal]` button and a content element. The native dialog manages keyboard dismissal, focus trapping, and background inertness; the controller adds backdrop dismissal. Give the dialog an accessible label with `aria-labelledby` and a corresponding heading inside each content template. Use `textContent` for user-supplied values.
+
+## Shared styles
+
+`styles.css` exposes design tokens on `:root` and three cascade layers (`base`, `components`, `layout`). Reuse `.button`, `.button-small`, `.button-outline`, `.text-button`, `.eyebrow`, `.badge`, `.info-box`, and `.dialog-form`. Use `<button>` for actions and `<a>` for navigation. The `.product-grid` and `.wrap` utilities provide responsive composition.
+
+## Application behavior
+
+`app.js` owns product data and composes these components. The cart is session-only. Profile storage uses localStorage and gracefully falls back to session state. Profile creation is a local demonstration, not authentication. Checkout, rewards tracking, contact channels, and location details require real service data before launch.
+
+Run locally with `pnpm start`.
